course: dictionary
lesson: 7790
title: A zebra that is gone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quagga is a noun, so it is a thing: an animal. The clues around it tell you what kind of animal it is. «The quagga was a zebra with stripes only on its front half.» Zebra tells you it is a striped animal like a horse, and the stripes on the front half tell you how it looked.
explain: «It was hunted out in South Africa, and the last died in a zoo in 1883.» Hunted out means people hunted the animals until none were left alive. Read the rest of the sentence, and you can tell that the quagga is no longer alive anywhere.
explain: Scientists use context too. «DNA showed the quagga was a kind of plains zebra.» DNA is the code inside every living thing that shows its family ties. The DNA showed that the quagga was not a separate kind of animal after all, but a type of plains zebra.
fact: A quagga is a kind of zebra from South Africa, with stripes only on the front half of its body and a plain brown back.
fact: «Extinct» means no living animals of that kind are left anywhere in the world.
fact: The quagga became extinct more than a hundred years ago, because people hunted it.
fact: The last quagga died in a zoo in 1883.
fact: DNA showed that the quagga was a type of plains zebra, and a project in South Africa is breeding zebras that look like quaggas again.
exercise: What is a quagga? | A rock animal related to elephants | *A kind of zebra from South Africa | A brown horse with no stripes at all | A kind of bird that lives in the Amsterdam zoo
exercise: «The quagga was a zebra with stripes only on its front half.» Which part of the quagga had stripes? | *The front half | The tail only | The back half | The legs only
exercise: «The quagga became extinct more than a hundred years ago.» What does extinct mean? | Found only in zoos | *No living ones are left anywhere in the world | Born again next year | Very large and strong
test: Why did the quagga become extinct? | *Because people hunted it until none were left | Because it turned into a different animal | Because it ran away to the mountains | Because it grew too big to eat
test: «DNA showed the quagga was a kind of plains zebra.» What did scientists learn from the DNA? | The quagga lived in the sea | The quagga was a type of elephant | The quagga had no stripes at all | *The quagga was a type of plains zebra
exam: The quagga is extinct, but a project is breeding zebras that look like quaggas again; what does this tell you? | *People are trying to bring back how the quagga looked | Quaggas were never real animals | Zebras have now become extinct | The quagga is still alive somewhere in South Africa
